@talks pool
topic: day
// TW1, the Talk a while pack: shared pool, topic day (their day, and yours).

== cold-tea
them: My day started with cold tea. Should've known.   #funny
them: Then it got better. It usually does after cold tea.
ask: How's your day been, honestly?
listen: What made it better?
  them: Someone said thank you, out of nowhere. Kept me going all afternoon.   #warm
share: Busy. I learned a lot, though.
  them: Busy and learning. That's a good day, that is.
cheer: Better now. I'm sitting down.
  them: Sitting down fixes most things. The rest, dinner fixes.   #funny

== nothing-wrong
them: Nothing went wrong today. Nothing at all.
them: Strangely tiring, that. You keep waiting for it.   #funny
ask: Do you like the quiet days, or the busy ones?
listen: What do you do on a quiet day?
  them: Tidy things that don't need it. Then tidy them again.   #funny
share: Busy. The time goes faster.
  them: It does. Then you look up and it's dinner.
cheer: Quiet. Quiet with biscuits.
  them: A connoisseur of quiet. Respect.   #funny

== good-one
them: Today was one of the good ones. Everything just worked.
them: I want to write it down so I remember it on a bad one.
ask: What makes a good day, for you?
listen: What went right?
  them: All of it. Small things, one after another. Like dominoes, but nice.
share: A job done properly. No re-checks.
  them: That's a proper answer. That's a Works answer.
cheer: Second helpings. Simple as that.
  them: Can't argue with that. Shouldn't try.   #funny

== tired
when: !who:rina|pell
them: Long day. Better now I've sat down.
them: My feet are telling me all about it.   #funny
ask: Are you sleeping all right? You look like you're keeping up.
listen: What kept you so busy?
  them: Everything at once, then nothing, then everything. Ship life.
share: Mostly. The bunk's comfier than it looks.
  them: Good. Sleep's the whole trick out here. Ask Rina.
cheer: I'm sleeping now. With my eyes open.
  them: Advanced technique. Pell will want lessons.   #funny

== morning-person
when: time:morning|afternoon
them: Are you a morning person? I'm trying to become one.
them: It's not going well. I'm told it takes years.   #funny
ask: When do you feel most awake?
listen: Why try to become one?
  them: Breakfast's best early. Fresh everything. Worth the pain.
share: Evenings. I come alive after dinner.
  them: Me too, secretly. Don't tell the morning lot.   #funny
cheer: Never. I'm a lifelong half-awake person.
  them: Honest, at least. Most of the ship's the same.   #funny

== evening
when: time:evening|night
them: This is my favourite bit of the day. Shift done, nothing due.
them: The ship goes soft round the edges in the evening.
ask: What do you do with your evenings?
listen: Soft how?
  them: The lights go warm. People sit longer. Voices go down a notch.
share: Still working that out. A bit of everything.
  them: Good. There's a lot on. Find the ones you like.
cheer: This. Talking. Apparently.
  them: Excellent choice. Ten out of ten.   #funny

== fixed-one
when: tier>=acquaintance
them: I fixed one thing today and three more broke. Typical.   #funny
them: Not my fault, any of them. Probably.
ask: Have you had a day like that yet?
listen: What broke?
  them: A drawer, a lamp and my patience. In that order.   #funny
share: Yes. Fixed one, found two.
  them: Welcome aboard. That's the Wren in one sentence.   #funny
cheer: Every day. I just call it Tuesday.
  them: Ha! Tuesday. I'll use that.   #funny

== thank-you
when: tier>=acquaintance !who:brennan
them: Someone thanked me today for something I did last month.
them: I'd forgotten it. They hadn't.   #warm
ask: Who's been kind to you lately?
listen: What had you done?
  them: Held a door with my foot while they carried a crate. Tiny thing.
share: Lots of people. Everyone's been kind.
  them: Good. Pass it on, that's how it works here.   #warm
cheer: Brennan. With biscuits.
  them: Brennan's kindness is mostly biscuits. It works.   #funny

== bad-start
when: tier>=colleague
them: I had a bad start today. Snapped at someone who didn't deserve it.
them: I said sorry at lunch. They said they'd forgotten. They hadn't.
ask: How do you fix a day that starts wrong?
listen: Are you two all right now?
  them: We are. Sitting together at dinner. That's how you know.   #warm
share: I talk to someone. Usually that does it.
  them: Like now? Good. It's working, a bit.   #warm
cheer: Start it again after lunch.
  them: The second-start rule. I like it.   #funny

== best-bit
when: tier>=friend
them: Do you know what the best bit of my day was?
them: This. Honestly. Sitting here with you.   #warm
ask: What was the best bit of yours?
listen: Really? Not dinner?
  them: Dinner's a close second. Don't tell Brennan.   #funny
share: This, as well. Truly.
  them: Then we're agreed. Same again tomorrow.   #warm
cheer: Finding out I'm better than dinner.
  them: Only just. Don't get big-headed.   #funny
